{
  "id": "murphy-shakti-60min-bilateral-amygdala-fast",
  "name": "Shakti 60-min bilateral session: amygdala signal (fast alternation)",
  "category": "spiritual",
  "evidence": "claim",
  "origin": "Todd Murphy (8 Coil Shakti)",
  "uT": 1,
  "summary": "Murphy's single 60-minute session 'to try to create an intense experience in ONE session': the amygdala burst-firing signal, his best-tested choice, over both temporal lobes on the 8 Coil Shakti crosses, with the two coil pairs taking turns every half-second (the vendor's fast alternation).",
  "setting": "Blindfold, earplugs or a sound-blocking headset (the vendor: 'substituting white noise won't work'), no interruptions and no plans afterwards. Murphy: 'For the first twenty minutes, not much happens.'",
  "schedule": "A one-off for a single intense experience, not a series (the vendor: repeating it 'might eventually elicit an unpleasant experience'); at most once every 3 weeks.",
  "notes": "Four coils in a cross over each temporal lobe, as in the 8 Coil Shakti chart: top C5/C6, bottom T9/T10, front FT7/FT8, back TP7/TP8. One stereo channel drives the top and bottom coils of both crosses, the other the front and back coils; the vendor says single long sessions 'should be bilateral'. The vendor's optional fast mode switches channels 'twice each second' and, it says, 'emerged as the most effective' in the original developers' lab tests; here (two tracks, the signal gated in point tables) the top and bottom coils and the front and back coils take turns every 0.5 s. So that the half-second clock and the signal repeat together, each burst comes every 4.5 s (latency 3.8 s instead of about 4 s), and the bursts alternately start on the top/bottom and on the front/back pair. murphy-shakti-60min-bilateral-amygdala-slow has the standard mode. Coil polarity follows the vendor's chart, one + and one − coil in each pair: on the left cross the top (C5) and front (FT7) coils are − and the bottom (T9) and back (TP7) coils +; on the right cross the top (C6) and front (FT8) coils are + and the bottom (T10) and back (TP8) coils −. The − coils have negative weights, which reverse their current as if the coil were turned over; + is taken as this helmet's normal drive. The amygdala ('burstx') file is proprietary; it is approximated by the built-in accelerating burst (6 to 30 Hz), 230 points at the vendor's standard 3-ms points (0.69 s). An independent randomized, sham-controlled study of the 8 Coil Shakti amygdala signal over both temporal lobes (30 min) found no effect on emotional responses (Gendle & McGrath 2012), and a double-blind God Helmet test found no field effect (Granqvist 2005). Persinger's lab reported more aggression and less trust after three weekly bilateral burst-firing sessions (Gillis & Persinger 1993). Not for people with epilepsy, seizure history or a psychiatric condition; stop on distress.",
  "targets": ["left-amygdala", "right-amygdala"],
  "source": "Murphy, Shakti demo: Two ways to use Shakti https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/two_ways.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: 60 minute sessions https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/hour.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Both temporal lobes https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/bi_temporal.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Getting started (8-coil chart; one test every 72 hours) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/getting_started_basic.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Understanding the 8 Coil Shakti (fast and slow alternation) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/rot_principles.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: 8 coil placement https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/8_coil_placement.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Using the 8 Coil Shakti over the temporal lobes https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/rot_temporal.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: What are 'Rapid' and 'High-Speed' signals? (3-ms points, 4-s latency) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/rapid_&_high_speed_signals.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Formal discussion (about 9.6 s of field per minute) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/mono_proposal.htm ; Ryczko & Persinger 2002, Percept Mot Skills 95:592 (230-point burst-firing pattern) https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12434855/ ; Gendle & McGrath 2012, Percept Mot Skills 114:217 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22582690/ ; Granqvist et al. 2005, Neurosci Lett 379:1 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15849873/ ; Gillis & Persinger 1993, Percept Mot Skills 76:168 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8451123/ ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Overcoming dud sessions (60-min sessions every 21 days) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/duds.htm",
